<title>INDIA: Indian silver rises on industrial demand.</title>
<headline>Indian silver rises on industrial demand.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Silver prices rose on industrial demand in early trading on Thursday but gold was quiet in lacklustre activity, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said recent rise in world silver prices pushed up the cost of imported silver and aided the upsurge.</p>
<p>Traders expect a pick up in demand for gold with the wedding season ahead but activity was dull for the time being.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) was steady at 58,800 rupees per piece in early trade, after rising 200 rupees on Wednesday.  </p>
